## Fairness by age (pre-registered, P5)

Dev out-of-fold scores (CV repeat r0) at the project threshold {{fair_threshold}}, four age bands, stratified bootstrap 95% intervals ({{fair_n_boot}} resamples). The holdout was not used. The rule was fixed before the results (`notes/00_preregistration.md`, A5): a gap between a band and all other rows counts as real only if its Bonferroni-adjusted interval ({{fair_n_comparisons}} comparisons) excludes 0.

{{fair_table_md}}

- **Gaps passing the rule: {{fair_n_real}} of {{fair_n_comparisons}}.** All are **{{fair_verdict}}**. This is **not** evidence that the model is fair: bands have only {{fair_fraud_min}}–{{fair_fraud_max}} fraud cases, and the widest adjusted interval spans {{fair_widest}}.
- At the unadjusted 95% level, {{fair_n_95}} gaps exclude 0: {{fair_hint}}. Where they point the same way, {{fair_direction}}. This is a lead to re-check on more data, not a finding.
- **Without `customer_age`:** PR-AUC {{noage_diff}} {{noage_ci}} ({{noage_verdict}}). Step-up rate changes for 18–29 ({{noage_young}}) and for 60+ ({{noage_old}}) (descriptive). Age ranks {{age_shap_rank}} features by mean |SHAP| ({{age_shap_share}} of the total). Dropping age is an option where using it is not acceptable.
- Age is the only person attribute in the data. No causal or legal claim is made; a real deployment needs its own fairness review on real data.

## Limitations and risks

- **Unknown provenance.** Patterns may be artefacts of how the data was generated (for example, no fraud below {{fraud_min_usd}} although {{legit_below_fraud_min}} of legitimate transactions are smaller; independent channel and device).
- **No customer or card ID.** No customer-level features; one customer may appear in train and validation, so CV can be optimistic by an unknown amount.
- **No real timestamps.** No out-of-time validation; temporal drift is untested.
- **Small positive class.** {{n_fraud}} fraud cases in total, {{ho_fraud}} in the holdout; holdout cost intervals are wide.
- **Assumed costs.** All cost numbers are illustrative; real costs differ by institution and change the threshold.
- **Fairness only partly assessed.** Age bands only (see above): gaps were not distinguishable with this data, which does not establish fairness. No other person attributes exist to check.
- **Probabilities.** Sigmoid and isotonic calibration did not improve the Brier score on CV (Brier {{lr_brier}}); calibration under drift was not checked.

